    "label": null,
    "prompt": "$LMN$ is a triangle. $\\overrightarrow{ML}=3\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ and $\\overrightarrow{NL}=\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b}$. Write in terms of $\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ and $\\underset{\\sim}{b}$:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p60-q5-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 60 p60-q5-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont},line width=0.8pt]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (L) at (0,0); \\coordinate (M) at (2,2); \\coordinate (N) at (4,0);\n\\draw (L)--(M)--(N)--cycle;\n\\draw[->] ($(M)!0.43!(L)$)--($(M)!0.56!(L)$);\n\\draw[->] ($(N)!0.43!(L)$)--($(N)!0.56!(L)$);\n\\path (M)--(L) node[midway,above left] {$3\\underset{\\sim}{a}$};\n\\path (N)--(L) node[midway,below] {$\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b}$};\n\\node[left] at (L) {$L$}; \\node[above] at (M) {$M$}; \\node[right] at (N) {$N$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
